# Environment
.env
.env.backup_*
.env.diff_*

# Superpowers
.superpowers/

# Go
bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# TLS certs (dev) — CONST-053 / §11.4.30: private keys/certs are never
# versioned. Regeneration mechanism (§11.4.77): scripts/gen_dev_certs.sh
# (self-signed, CN=helixllm, dev-only). See certs/README.md.
# NOTE: intentionally file-glob (*.pem / *.key), not a `certs/` directory
# ignore — a directory-level ignore would also hide certs/README.md from
# git, and negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# itself excluded.
*.pem
*.key
!certs/README.md

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Anchored to repo root so build artefact `./helixllm` is ignored,
# but the `cmd/helixllm/` source directory remains trackable
# (round-95 CONST-046 i18n migration added a test file there).
/helixllm

# round-295 — stray `go build ./challenges/runner/` artefact at
# repo root if the runner is built without -o. Source under
# `challenges/runner/` remains trackable; only the root binary
# named `runner` is ignored (anchored).
/runner

# Phase-4 vision (VLM) boot harness — `go build ./cmd/visiongen-boot/`
# without -o (or the vision_boot_test.sh helper) drops the built binary
# at the repo root as `./visiongen-boot`. Source under
# `cmd/visiongen-boot/` remains trackable; only the root-level binary
# is ignored (anchored), per §11.4.30 no-versioned-build-artifacts.
/visiongen-boot

# Serving Phase-1 pre-boot config validator — `go build
# ./cmd/laneconfig-validate/...` without -o drops the built binary at
# the repo root as `./laneconfig-validate`. Source under
# `cmd/laneconfig-validate/` remains trackable; only the root-level
# binary is ignored (anchored), per §11.4.30 no-versioned-build-artifacts.
/laneconfig-validate

# Serving Phase-2 agent-gen (Lane-B / ClassAgent) boot harness — `go build
# -o cmd/agentgen-boot/agentgen-boot ./cmd/agentgen-boot/` drops the built
# binary in-directory. Source under `cmd/agentgen-boot/` remains trackable;
# only the compiled binary is ignored (anchored), per §11.4.30.
/cmd/agentgen-boot/agentgen-boot

# Vectorize service (§11.4.107 vtracer capability) — `go build .` without
# -o inside services/vectorize/ names the binary after the module
# (`dev.helix.llm.services.vectorize`, from services/vectorize/go.mod)
# rather than the directory. Source under `services/vectorize/` remains
# trackable; only this module-named build artefact is ignored (anchored),
# per §11.4.30. Regeneration mechanism (§11.4.77): `go build -o
# dev.helix.llm.services.vectorize .` from services/vectorize/ (same
# module the sibling vectorize-shim/vtracer .gitignore entries already
# cover for the other two build outputs of this service).
/services/vectorize/dev.helix.llm.services.vectorize

# Python bytecode + tool caches for the in-tree services (imagegen, videogen,
# vectorize, tts, audio, container). The Go side of this file is exhaustive and
# the Python side was empty, though six services ship Python: `__pycache__/`
# directories already exist in all six working trees, none of them ignored and
# none yet tracked. That is one careless `git add -A` away from versioning
# build output, which is exactly the class §11.4.30 / CONST-053 forbids —
# caught during a §11.4.84 quiescence check, before anything landed.
#
# Regeneration mechanism (§11.4.77): none required. CPython rewrites
# `__pycache__/*.pyc` from the adjacent `.py` source on next import, and each
# tool recreates its own cache on next run. Deleting any of these costs a
# single re-import.
#
# Unanchored on purpose: unlike the build artefacts above — which are ignored
# at a fixed path so the identically-named SOURCE directory stays trackable —
# these names are never source anywhere in the tree, at any depth.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
